Tests exist and are fairly complete (coverage was 100%). The problem is pure complexity (CC 18 → CRAP 18 even at full coverage). The refactor: extract pure helpers. I'll also export them for direct tests (file already exports action, STRATEGIES, findRepoEntry — adding exports follows gitPushGuard's pattern but this file exports less... I'll add the new helpers to exports so tests can hit them directly; it's additive and consistent with the repo's other modules).

Refactor:

```js
function resolveCustomParams(params) {
   return params.customParams ||
       (params.jobParams && params.jobParams.customParams) ||
       {};
}

function buildTargetRepository(repoName, entry, customParams) {
   var targetRepository = { repo: repoName };
   if (!entry) {
       console.warn('resolveRepoFromTicket: repo "' + repoName +
           '" not found in repositories file — forwarding repoName only');
       return targetRepository;
   }
   if (entry.branch)     targetRepository.baseBranch = entry.branch;
   if (entry.gitlabGroup) targetRepository.owner     = entry.gitlabGroup;
   // workingDir: explicit entry.workingDir → or derive from dependenciesDir/repoName
   // (checkout.sh clones repos into ./dependencies/{repo}/ by default)
   var dependenciesDir = customParams.dependenciesDir || './dependencies';
   targetRepository.workingDir = entry.workingDir || (dependenciesDir + '/' + repoName);
   console.log('resolveRepoFromTicket: repo entry found — branch=' +
       (entry.branch || 'n/a') + ', owner=' + (entry.gitlabGroup || 'n/a') +
       ', workingDir=' + targetRepository.workingDir);
   return targetRepository;
}

function publishTargetRepository(params, targetRepository) {
   // Mutate params so configLoader and preCliDevelopmentSetup pick it up downstream.
   // configLoader.loadProjectConfig is called as loadProjectConfig(params.jobParams || params),
   // so we write into both locations to cover both the Teamate and JSRunner call paths.
   if (!params.customParams) params.customParams = {};
   params.customParams.targetRepository = targetRepository;
   if (params.jobParams) {
       if (!params.jobParams.customParams) params.jobParams.customParams = {};
       params.jobParams.customParams.targetRepository = targetRepository;
   }

function action(params) {
   var ticket = params.ticket;
   if (!ticket) {
       console.warn('resolveRepoFromTicket: no ticket in params — skipping repo resolution');
       return true;
   }

   var customParams = resolveCustomParams(params);
   var strategyName = customParams.repoNameStrategy || 'fromSummary';
   var strategy = STRATEGIES[strategyName];
   if (!strategy) {
       console.warn('resolveRepoFromTicket: unknown strategy "' + strategyName +
           '" — available: ' + Object.keys(STRATEGIES).join(', ') + '. Skipping.');
       return true;
   }

   var repoName = strategy(ticket, customParams);
   if (!repoName) {
       console.warn('resolveRepoFromTicket: strategy "' + strategyName +
           '" could not resolve repo name from ticket ' + ticket.key + ' — skipping.');
       return true;
   }

   console.log('resolveRepoFromTicket: resolved repo "' + repoName +
       '" from ticket ' + ticket.key + ' via strategy "' + strategyName + '"');

   var entry = findRepoEntry(repoName, customParams.repositoriesFile);
   publishTargetRepository(params, buildTargetRepository(repoName, entry, customParams));

   return true;
}
``

CC counts: action = 1 + 3 ifs + 1 (|| in strategyName) = 5; buildTargetRepository = 1 + 3 = 4; publishTargetRepository = 1 + 3 = 4; resolveCustomParams = 1 + 2 = 3. All ≤ 8 at full coverage ✓.

Order parity: original order = findRepoEntry → console.log (resolved repo) happens BEFORE findRepoEntry... wait original: log "resolved repo" THEN findRepoEntry THEN build. My version: log → findRepoEntry → build (logs inside) → publish. Same order ✓.

Characterization tests: coverage already 100% — existing tests cover all branches. New tests for helpers directly:
- resolveCustomParams: params.customParams wins; jobParams.customParams fallback; {} default.
- buildTargetRepository: full entry (branch+gitlabGroup+workingDir); entry without branch/gitlabGroup; no entry → repo-only; custom dependenciesDir.
- publishTargetRepository: creates params.customParams when missing; jobParams path; both.

TDD: write helper tests first (RED — helpers don't exist), then refactor (GREEN). Since these tests call mod.resolveCustomParams which doesn't exist yet, they'd fail with "not a function". Let me write tests + refactor in sequence: tests first, run (expect failures), then refactor, run (green).

